            <ArticleTitle>Serum lipid profiles and the presence of yellow plaque in coronary lesions in vivo.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>676-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary angioscopy was used to examine the relation between plaque color and serum lipid levels in 44 patients with yellow plaque and 94 with white plaque. The findings indicate a strong relation between lipid profile and plaque color and therefore between lipid profile and plaque composition in vivo.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
